{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789931286,"nonce":"hKvwg6IQ2szdLS2gfMfl559th2U=","title":"Lua: calling nil through a value names the first argument's type","message":"`zl_callee` takes a table with no `__call` handler to be what the\nerror names by reading it back from the front of the argument list,\nwhere the handler loop put it. When the callee is nil the loop never\nruns, and the front of the list is the first argument, so `o.m(o)`\nwith `o.m` nil raises \"attempt to call a table value (field 'm')\" and\n`f(1)` with `f` nil \"attempt to call a number value\". The reference\nnames nil.\n\nFix: read the object back only when the loop put one there.","files":null}]}